CapabilitiesRegistry
├── constructor
│   ├── stores the curator owner and configured protocol proposer
│   └── inherits zero-owner validation and accepts a missing proposer
├── initCapability
│   ├── rejects callers other than the curator owner
│   ├── rejects unregistered or changed code
│   ├── rejects changed, reordered, duplicate, zero, or empty selectors
│   └── copies the immutable manifest without authorizing an adapter
├── acceptCapability
│   ├── protocol proposal alone never accepts on the curator's behalf
│   ├── requires an active proposal for this exact registry, adapter, and implementation
│   ├── rejects even identical code at an unapproved implementation address
│   ├── atomically copies the manifest and records local consent
│   └── failed acceptance rolls back a newly copied manifest
├── setWhitelistedStatus
│   ├── approval requires a local manifest, active proposal, and unchanged code
│   ├── revocation is available for any pair, even if the proposer is unavailable
│   └── ownership transfer changes acceptance authority without changing manifests
├── isWhitelisted
│   ├── installation requires both protocol proposal and curator consent
│   ├── withdrawal or code changes prevent future installation
│   ├── reproposal of unchanged code preserves earlier curator consent
│   └── reproposal never restores curator-revoked consent
├── immutable manifest reads
│   ├── remain available after withdrawal, revocation, or proposer unavailability
│   └── are independent across curator registries and returned memory copies
└── stateful fuzzing
    └── interleaved proposal, withdrawal, acceptance, revocation, and code changes match an independent model
